Third-party licenses
====================

Rebrew's own source is MIT. See LICENSE.

The optional dependencies below use other grants. Each one ships its own
license text. The expressions match the revisions pinned in uv.lock.
``make sbom`` writes them into ``dist/rebrew.cdx.json``.

The grant every other pinned distribution declares is recorded in
``tools/licenses.py`` and emitted per component in the SBOM, so the released
inventory answers "what license is this under" for the whole tree and not
only for the copyleft entries below.

similarity group — resembl
--------------------------

resembl 2.0.0 (sibling checkout ``../resembl``,
https://github.com/maci0/resembl) declares ``License: GPLv3``. That is
GPL-3.0-only: GNU GPL version 3, and the upstream declaration has no
later-version clause. ``make setup`` installs this group through the path
dependency in ``[dependency-groups]`` / ``[tool.uv.sources]``. Wheel
Requires-Dist stays limited to packages that resolve on PyPI.

m2c group — m2c
---------------

m2c commit aa869da289a565c68f701e734bd74606f1bd5ed4
(https://github.com/matt-kempster/m2c) declares
``License-Expression: GPL-3.0-only``. Install with ``uv sync --group m2c``.
The pin lives in ``[dependency-groups]``, same as resembl, so Requires-Dist
leaves it out.

prove extra — pyvex (via angr)
------------------------------
angr 9.3.4 is BSD-2-Clause. Its dependency pyvex 9.3.4 declares
``License-Expression: BSD-2-Clause AND GPL-2.0-or-later``. The Python
bindings are BSD-2-Clause, copyright 2015 The Regents of the University
of California. LibVEX, included in that distribution, is GPL-2.0-or-later
(``vex/LICENSE.GPL`` and ``vex/LICENSE.README``). ``rebrew[prove]``
installs this tree.

binsync extra — declib
----------------------

declib 4.5.0 declares ``License-Expression: BSD-2-Clause``. It pulls
``pyghidra`` 3.1.0 (Apache-2.0) and ``prompt-toolkit`` 3.0.53, whose
metadata carries only the trove text ``OSI Approved :: BSD License``; the
SBOM records that string verbatim rather than choosing a clause count the
artifact does not state. ``rebrew[binsync]`` installs this tree.

Every resolve: certifi and hypothesis
------------------------------------

certifi 2026.7.22 declares ``License: MPL-2.0`` (free-text field, no PEP 639
expression) and hypothesis 6.168.0 declares ``License-Expression: MPL-2.0``.
MPL-2.0 is file-level reciprocal: it obliges a distributor of a *modified*
file to publish that file's source under MPL-2.0. Rebrew vendors neither
package's files nor any modification of them; both are installed unmodified
from their own wheels, which already carry the licence text, so the grant
Rebrew redistributes here is the original MPL-2.0 one. The two entries are
listed so a consumer reading ``dist/rebrew.cdx.json`` can trace that grant
back to its origin. ``tests/test_packaging.py`` fails when the resolved
environment holds a copyleft package missing from
``tools/generate_sbom._COPYLEFT_EXPRESSIONS``.
